> Full-width values, strict streams and capture limits

For UINT64_MAX, k=63: the word contains 63 zeros and 64 payload
ones, 127 characters in total. Counting zeros never needs a 64-bit
shift; the encoder's largest payload shift is 63. The saved old-header
sanitizer probe reaches an invalid shift exponent 64 at 2^63. The
new implementation supports both 2^63 and UINT64_MAX directly.

The whole input alphabet is validated first. An unfinished zero prefix
or payload is an error; trailing zeros are not padding. A prefix longer
than 63 would require a value outside uint64 and raises overflow.
Previously, inputs such as 01 were accepted as a smaller value, x
was accepted as one, and sequence encoding silently omitted zero.
Those invalid-input behaviours are corrected. Empty input remains the
valid encoding of an empty sequence, and every valid legacy encoding
is preserved.

An owned trace stores B bit characters, N values and N word records,
so its logical retained cost is C=B+2N. Encoding checks the complete
known cost before copies or emission. Decoding reserves B before owned
copying, then two entries per complete word before appending its value
and span. It can consume a word before reaching that quota check.
Scalar fields, runtime/result temporaries, string/vector capacity and
allocator bytes are excluded; the cap is not a peak-memory or CPU-time
bound. It defaults to one million; zero disables only the optional
quota. Arithmetic checks remain, and failure exposes no partial result.
Ordinary and work-only calls have no optional capture quota or history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/elias_gamma_boundaries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto maximum=std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();const auto t=dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_encode_trace({maximum});const auto back=dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_decode_trace(t.bits);
  std::print("Full range: 2^63 length {}; UINT64_MAX length {}; maximum round trip {}; capture entries {}.\n",dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_code_length(std::uint64_t{1}<<63),t.bits.size(),back.values==t.values,t.captured_entries);
  std::print("Maximum spans: prefix [{},{}); payload [{},{}); actual payload ones {}.\n",t.words.at(0).begin,t.words.at(0).payload_begin,t.words.at(0).payload_begin,t.words.at(0).end,std::count(t.bits.begin()+t.words.at(0).payload_begin,t.bits.end(),'1'));
  int malformed=0;for(const std::string bits:{"0","000","01","001","0100","x","0x","10x"})try{(void)dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_decode(bits);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++malformed;}
  int zeros=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_encode_one(0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++zeros;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_encode({1,0,2});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++zeros;}
  int wide=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_decode(std::string(64,'0')+"1"+std::string(64,'0'));}catch(const std::overflow_error&){++wide;}
  std::print("Malformed legacy-stream rejections {}/8; zero-value rejections {}/2; overwide-prefix rejections {}/1.\n",malformed,zeros,wide);
  const auto e=dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_encode_trace({13},9),d=dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_decode_trace(e.bits,9);int caps=0;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_encode_trace({13},8);}catch(const std::length_error&){++caps;}
  for(std::size_t cap:{6,8})try{(void)dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_decode_trace(e.bits,cap);}catch(const std::length_error&){++caps;}
  std::print("Exact encoding/decoding entries {}/{}; disabled-cap entries {}; base/one-short rejections {}/3.\n",e.captured_entries,d.captured_entries,dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_decode_trace(e.bits,0).captured_entries,caps);
  std::print("Empty encoding entries {}; empty decoding values {}.\n",dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_encode_trace({}).captured_entries,dm::algorithms::elias_gamma_decode("").size());
  const auto& w=t.words.at(0);dm::graphics::Diagram g(64,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.5;box.height=1.7;box.font_size=23;box.fill={191,219,254};
  g.node("prefix",{0,0},std::format("prefix zeros\n[{},{})\n{} bits",w.begin,w.payload_begin,w.payload_begin-w.begin),box);box.fill={187,247,208};
  g.node("payload",{6,0},std::format("binary payload\n[{},{})\n{} ones",w.payload_begin,w.end,w.end-w.payload_begin),box);box.fill={254,215,170};
  g.node("value",{12,0},std::format("value\n{}\n{} coded bits",w.value,w.end-w.begin),box).edge("prefix","payload").edge("payload","value","decode")
   .text({6,2.6},"Full-width value: every payload shift stays below 64",26).save_svg("build/elias_gamma_boundaries.svg");
}
